// Phone component - a text field for a phone number, rendered as <input type="tel">: a mobile browser shows
// the phone keypad, and the 'tel' autocomplete token lets the browser offer the visitor's saved number.
// fmdbmix:textField makes the field a conditional-logic source with the text operators, and has the server
// check the length bounds and the pattern the browser checks.
// The default pattern accepts an optional leading '+', then digits, spaces, dots, hyphens and parentheses,
// with 6 to 15 digits (the E.164 maximum). The browser compiles a pattern with the 'v' flag, which refuses
// '(', ')' and '-' unescaped in a character class; the CND lexer reads '\\' in a quoted value as one '\'.
// checkFormat set to false turns the check off, in the view and on the server; the pattern stays mandatory.
[fmdbext:phone] > jnt:content, fmdbmix:element, fmdbmix:submittableField, fmdbmix:profileMappableField, fmdbmix:textField, fmdbmix:textValidationMessages
 - helpText (string, richtext[ckeditor.toolbar='FormidableHelp',ckeditor.customConfig='$context/modules/formidable-engine/javascript/ckeditor/helpTextConfig.js']) i18n indexed=no
 - required (boolean) = false
 - placeholder (string) i18n indexed=no
 - defaultValue (string) i18n indexed=no
 - checkFormat (boolean) = true autocreated
 - pattern (string) = '(?=(?:\\D*\\d){6,15}\\D*$)\\+?[\\d .\\(\\)\\-]+' autocreated mandatory indexed=no
 - minLength (long)
 - maxLength (long)
 // Simple string: 'tel' (default), 'off', or any HTML5 autocomplete token ('tel-national', 'work tel'...)
 - autocomplete (string) = 'tel' autocreated indexed=no
